;;; **A keyword pair below a form: refused at the parse.**
;;;
;;; `examples/syntax/trace-steps.ein` with its `trace` written `tracex`, a
;;; mutation of the engine fuzzer's `no-crash` property; the note is
;;; `corpus/fuzz_findings/kwpair-below-the-filter.md`. `tracex` is neither a
;;; kernel head nor a declared relation, so the form would be an ontology
;;; fact, and its `(step …)` arguments hold keyword pairs.
;;;
;;; Two render views label a form's arguments with `dot_util::value_label`,
;;; which would recurse into each `(step …)` and reach its keyword pairs:
;;;
;;;   ein render constraints  — `constraints.rs` filters a declaration's own
;;;                             keyword pairs, one level deep
;;;   ein render program      — `ir_dot`'s ontology path, with no filter
;;;
;;; Neither reaches one: a value holds no keyword pair, since no keyword pair
;;; parses inside a term or a nested fact (Q-M1e2.28). The grammar refuses
;;; this file at its first `:rule`, and its `.expected` is the parse report.
;;; The corpus runs every view over it, and each meets the refusal.
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;

(tracex (step s1 :rule from-condition :using (c10) :derives (lives-in N H1))
  (step s2 :rule adjacent :using (and s1 c15) :derives (color-loc Blue H2))
  (step s3 :using (s2))
  (step s4 :derives (final X)))
